  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only (pca_n2000, single) achieves 48.5% acc while image-only (resnet50, single) achieves only 20.8% acc—essentially at chance level. This raises a critical uncertainty: is the image modality fundamentally uninformative for this task, or was resnet50 simply an inadequate encoder? Question tested: config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) directly probes whether a substantially stronger, pretrained vision transformer can extract meaningful signal from the images. Why this is the best next experiment: The answer to this question gates the entire multimodal search space (configs 016–051). If ViT-L lifts image accuracy meaningfully (e.g., >35%), multimodal fusion becomes a high-value direction worth exploring. If it remains near chance, we can confidently deprioritize image and multimodal configs, redirecting limited budget toward RNA encoder improvements (scgpt, scvi) and multiprofile aggregation. This single experiment maximally reduces strategic uncertainty before committing to a large sub-space of configurations."
